[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/Lichess"]
[FEN "2r5/8/4k3/8/1P6/1K1R4/8/8 b - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2022.07.06"]
[UTCTime "15:56:50"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ A frontal defense is best used when the pawn has not advanced to the 5th rank. Despite the Black king being two files away from the passed pawn, the game is still salvageable. Black survives by giving a barrage of checks, preventing the white king from making progress.

First, we need to prevent white from playing b5 right away. }
1... Rb8 2. Ka4 { Now, we can start the sequence of checks and white will not be able to do anything. } 2... Ra8+ 3. Kb5 Rb8+ 4. Kc5 Rc8+ 5. Kb6 Rb8+ { White has no options but to defend the pawn. } 6. Ka5 Ra8+ 7. Kb5 Rb8+ { White can't make any progress. The game will eventually end in a draw. } *


