{ We covered all the Rook and Pawn vs Rook positions, the next 4 chapters are about a rook vs one or more pawns.

This position comes from Dvoretsky's endgames manual. The idea is to bring the king in a way that black's promotion to a queen doesn't come with a check, so white can checkmate black with the rook. }
1. Kc4 a2 2. Kb3! a1=Q { White would still be winning even if black would have promoted to a knight with check. } 3. Rh1# *


