{ The key idea is to park the king on h7 and advance the g-pawn. If we try to advance the h-pawn we will actually be too slow. }
1. Kg6 (1. g6 { Doesn't work due to the intermediate move Rh5+. Remember this resource! } { [%cal Rh1h5] }) 1... Kc7 2. Kh7 (2. Kg7 { This doesn't work because black's king will come to f5 just in time. }) 2... Kd7 3. g6 Ke7 4. g7 { One of the two pawns will eventually promote to a queen. } *


